y_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20135, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DJ3rqRhnm6EinnozxnHksY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20135, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01SfwGcELMMn7eMWivN788sw", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20435, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01SfwGcELMMn7eMWivN788sw", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20435, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SfwGcELMMn7eMWivN788sw", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25519, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017F5tjm1yKBHZsoriEf8kfr", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions after it was deployed (error rate 18%, status unhealthy). Its staging build, v2.3.1-rc, had also been marked unhealthy. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east was done, which briefly left the regions on mixed versions (us-east on v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second attempt finished successfully. All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and check why v2.3.1 went to production after its staging build was unhealthy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56119, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017F5tjm1yKBHZsoriEf8kfr", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56119, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017F5tjm1yKBHZsoriEf8kfr", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 59818, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EvLdBgcL1wHjKR7v6YEEe8", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 60118, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EvLdBgcL1wHjKR7v6YEEe8", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 60118, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EvLdBgcL1wHjKR7v6YEEe8", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 65150, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident for it (INC-0001).\n\n**Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1, the current release, was unhealthy, and its staging build v2.3.1-rc had also failed.\n- The first attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error. Only us-east moved to v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- I ran the rollback again and it finished. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0.\n- checkout-api now reports healthy, and its error rate has dropped from 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's only one and the on-call engineer was paged only once. The incident describes the failure, both rollback attempts and the current state. It also lists three follow-ups:\n- Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n- Find out why v2.3.1 went to production even though its staging build was unhealthy.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012SMzzzJo5eyp7NnkqNiwss", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015LjczfBcfNkyFD6sTmhEDt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MFpsyEXJpSSN5xEuxjKGpL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01AX4HYW4rteC7FFWpt5irTF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback only partly worked: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Trying the rollback once more:", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QNEubfX1kveacfPuYePJ2i", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DJ3rqRhnm6EinnozxnHksY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SfwGcELMMn7eMWivN788sw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017F5tjm1yKBHZsoriEf8kfr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all production regions after it was deployed (error rate 18%, status unhealthy). Its staging build, v2.3.1-rc, had also been marked unhealthy. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east was done, which briefly left the regions on mixed versions (us-east on v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second attempt finished successfully. All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback, and check why v2.3.1 went to production after its staging build was unhealthy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EvLdBgcL1wHjKR7v6YEEe8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident for it (INC-0001).\n\n**Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1, the current release, was unhealthy, and its staging build v2.3.1-rc had also failed.\n- The first attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error. Only us-east moved to v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- I ran the rollback again and it finished. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0.\n- checkout-api now reports healthy, and its error rate has dropped from 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's only one and the on-call engineer was paged only once. The incident describes the failure, both rollback attempts and the current state. It also lists three follow-ups:\n- Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.\n- Find out why v2.3.1 went to production even though its staging build was unhealthy.", "type": "text"}]}]}